From c07e8725ed2d41367dbb734bbe884750aff1cda0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:41:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-3-0103: own unchanged-holder native replay

Start native opcode compilation at command zero for every holder instead of selecting a path by object-count threshold. Preserve one ordered bytecode containing canonical PDFium barriers and exact owned native commands.

Validate the source mutation epoch once before replay, resolve optional-content visibility once per recorded run, and execute native geometry, paint, clip, and color without re-entering CPDF_PageObject for each command. Keep live object lookups only for canonical barriers and exceptional device fallback.

Treat a top-level non-group page as a direct Darken context even though CPDF_Page initializes the isolated bit. Actual groups, nested rendering, printing, Type3, mutation drift, and unsupported device paths remain fail-closed.

The representation remains bounded by the existing 96 MiB program budget and adds no per-page-object storage or render-loop synchronization.
---
 core/fpdfapi/page/veloce_render_program.cpp   |  42 ++--
 core/fpdfapi/page/veloce_render_program.h     |  17 +-
 .../page/veloce_render_program_unittest.cpp   |  76 +++---
 core/fpdfapi/render/cpdf_renderstatus.cpp     | 219 +++++++++---------
 4 files changed, 168 insertions(+), 186 deletions(-)

